.DS_Store
.venv/
__pycache__/
data/*.geojson
data/*.json
data/weather_cache_*.json
out/*.npy
out/*.png
# derived caches: regenerated in ~45 s by server/engine.attach_tsurf(), 166 MB each
# as rasters. These were NOT covered by out/*.npy and 1.7 GB of them had accumulated.
out/*.npz
out/v2/
out/v2_winter/
out/v2_cold/
!data/connectors.json
!out/grid.json

# Downloaded ground-truth tables: 172 MB, re-fetched by validate_sensors.fetch_all().
# microclimate_sensors.csv alone is 162 MB, over GitHub's 100 MB per-file hard limit.
data/*.csv
# Built by scripts/build_graph.py; 18 MB each and regenerable.
out/*.pkl
out/*.pkl.bak

# Provenance outputs: both are DERIVED and deliberately not stored. The digest cache is
# keyed on (size, mtime) and rebuilds itself; the ladder results rebuild from the DSMs in
# ~40 s. Checking a baseline in is what created the moving-yardstick problem in the first
# place -- see the Provenance section of ENGINE_CONTRACT.md.
out/.provenance_cache.json
out/bench_shade_ladder*.json

# The fitted Open-Meteo bias table IS checked in (~6 KB). It is derived, but it cannot be
# regenerated from anything in this repo: the fit needs microclimate_sensors.csv, which is
# 162 MB and excluded above. Leaving it out means a fresh clone silently serves the raw
# uncorrected feed -- exactly the failure server/weather.py reports `bias_mode` to prevent.
!data/openmeteo_bias.json

# Hand-authored, not derived: opening hours for the protected network. Nothing in the
# repo can regenerate it -- OSM carries opening_hours on 2 of 1232 indoor ways, so the
# table is written by hand and losing it means the availability gate silently degrades
# to "everything is always open", which is the bug it exists to fix.
!data/indoor_hours.json

# Shade sets generated on demand for a request date (server/engine.ensure_shade_set).
# ~350 MB each, regenerated in ~13 s, pruned to SHADEME_SHADE_CACHE.
out/day_*/
# Fetched reference data for the weather-source evaluations.
data/isd/
data/radiation/
data/openmeteo_sites/
